@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Rsync Transfer
  "Uploads local files to the VPS through the rsync binary with optional SSH transport."

  Provides:
    - remote.Rsync @source("symbol:Rsync")
    - remote.RsyncRequest @source("symbol:RsyncRequest")
    - remote.CompareDryRunRequest @source("symbol:CompareDryRunRequest")
    - remote.RsyncProgress @source("symbol:RsyncProgress")
    - remote.ProcessResult @source("symbol:ProcessResult")
    - remote.ProcessRunner @source("symbol:ProcessRunner")
    - remote.NewRsync @source("symbol:NewRsync")
    - remote.NewRsyncWithRunner @source("symbol:NewRsyncWithRunner")
    - remote.Rsync.Upload @source("symbol:Upload")
    - remote.Rsync.CompareDryRun @source("symbol:CompareDryRun")
    - remote.RsyncDestinationFromTarget @source("symbol:RsyncDestinationFromTarget")

  Consumes:
    - remote.SSHOptions
    - config.Target

  Invariants:
    - Upload MUST validate that the local source path exists before invoking rsync
    - CompareDryRun MUST use dry-run, itemize-changes, and stats without transferring bytes
    - CompareDryRun MUST request non-human-readable stats so counts and byte totals are plain integers
    - RsyncDestinationFromTarget MUST format an SSH rsync destination as user, host, and remote path
    - Progress callbacks MUST receive parsed lines when rsync progress output is present
    - Filters MUST be passed to rsync as --filter rules in the given order, identically for Upload and CompareDryRun
    - Rsync MUST NOT impose filters of its own; exclusion policy belongs to callers (a shared single file may be a dotfile)

  OutOfScope:
    - Deploy plan parsing and aggregation (owned by internal/deploy)
    - Remote manifest updates after upload (callers record blobs separately)

  Scenario (happy-path): Upload file
    Given a readable local source and rsync destination
    When Upload runs
    Then rsync exits 0 and ProcessResult captures output

  Scenario (happy-path): Compare dry-run
    Given a local directory and rsync destination
    When CompareDryRun runs
    Then rsync exits 0 with itemized change and stats output

  Scenario (negative): Missing source
    Given a non-existent local path
    When Upload runs
    Then it returns a validation error before spawning rsync
